---
title: Why I still build what I design
date: 2026-08-28
summary: Designing and building the same product removes the gap where most good ideas get lost.
tag: Build
color: mint
---

Every hand-off is a chance for something to get lost: a spacing rule, a hover state, the reason a button sits where it does.

## Constraints are design material

When I build, I see the real constraints early: content that's longer than expected, slow connections, awkward screen sizes. Those constraints make the design better, not worse.

## Fewer meetings, faster loops

When the designer can change the code, a small fix takes minutes instead of a ticket and a sprint.

## It's not either/or

I still work happily with development teams. Knowing how things get built just makes me a better partner to them.
